Resume requestId: a fresh id per ask, never recycled while a native packet can arrive

Codex review of #37: uniqueness only while asks are pending lets ask A finish
(reply/timeout or a closed connection), B reuse A's id on another connection,
and A's late native refusal land on B. An app now gives every resume ask a
fresh requestId (a UUID per ask) and never reuses it across connections and
reconnects while that ask's native packet could still arrive. A closed
connection records nothing by itself; its ask stays answerable by its own
native refusal only. Shared askAttribution vectors pin the orders, with a
reference ledger that fails on a recycled id, and an extension VM regression
holds A's native packet across a reconnect and a fresh ask B.

